  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is the current best at 0.619 acc / 0.610 F1, outperforming RNA-only multiprofile avgpool (0.591) by ~2.8%. We have clear evidence that avgpool > transformer and multiprofile > singleprofile, but the fusion strategy (concat vs. weighted) is the one untested variable in this exact neighborhood. Question: Does weighted fusion outperform simple concatenation when combining a dominant RNA signal (pca_n2000) with a weaker image signal (resnet50, image-only acc only 0.208)? This is the most informative next step because it is a clean single-variable A/B test against the current best, directly tests whether the fusion mechanism can further exploit the asymmetric modality strengths, and if it succeeds, provides an immediate improvement to the best configuration. If it does not, we confirm concat is sufficient and can redirect budget toward RNA encoder or image encoder upgrades with confidence."
}

